<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
  <title>{{ report.name }} — Draft Recommendations</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="../../../style.css">
</head>
<body class="mode-dynasty">
<div class="container">
  <header class="site">
    <h1>Draft Recommendations</h1>
    <div class="tagline">
      {{ report.name }} &middot; {{ report.season }} rookie draft &middot;
      {{ report.draft.num_teams }} teams &middot;
      {{ report.draft.rookie_pool_size }} available prospects
    </div>
    <nav>
      <a href="../">&larr; Back to league</a>
      {% if report.trades %}&middot; <a href="../trades/">Trade ideas</a>{% endif %}
      {% if report.waivers %}&middot; <a href="../waivers/">Waiver wire</a>{% endif %}
      <span class="muted small">&middot; Generated {{ report.generated_at }}</span>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <p class="muted small" style="margin-top: 0.5rem;">
    For each of your pick slots, we project which prospects will fall to you
    using a strict "best player available by FantasyCalc dynasty value"
    model. Real drafts have positional runs and reaches, so this is a starting
    point — not a guarantee.
  </p>

  {% macro prospect_row(p) %}
  <article class="prospect-row">
    <div class="prospect-rank">#{{ p.projected_rank }}</div>
    <div class="prospect-main">
      <span class="trade-player-name">{{ p.name }}</span>
      <span class="pos-tag">{{ p.position }}{% if p.team %} · {{ p.team }}{% endif %}</span>
      {% if p.injury_status %}<span class="injury Q">{{ p.injury_status }}</span>{% endif %}
      <div class="muted small">
        {% if p.age %}age {{ p.age | round | int }} &middot; {% endif %}
        dyn <strong>{{ p.dynasty_value | money }}</strong>
        {% if p.redraft_value %}&middot; redraft {{ p.redraft_value | money }}{% endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
  {% endmacro %}

  {% for slot in report.draft.my_slots %}
  <section class="draft-slot">
    <header class="draft-slot-header">
      <div>
        <h2>Pick {{ slot.label }}
          <span class="muted small">— overall #{{ slot.overall }}</span>
        </h2>
        <div class="muted small">
          Round {{ slot.round }}, slot {{ slot.slot_in_round }} of {{ report.draft.num_teams }}
          {% if slot.fc_value %}
          &middot; FantasyCalc slot value <strong>{{ slot.fc_value | money }}</strong>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>
    <p class="muted small">
      Projected board when you're on the clock — top {{ slot.projected_available | length }}
      prospects estimated to be available at overall pick {{ slot.overall }}.
    </p>
    {% for p in slot.projected_available %}{{ prospect_row(p) }}{% endfor %}
  </section>
  {% endfor %}

  {% if report.draft.later_board %}
  <section class="draft-slot draft-later">
    <h2>Falling beyond your last pick <span class="muted small">({{ report.draft.later_board | length }})</span></h2>
    <p class="muted small">
      Prospects projected to go later than your latest pick. Useful for trade-back
      decisions or eyeing late-round value.
    </p>
    {% for p in report.draft.later_board %}{{ prospect_row(p) }}{% endfor %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <div class="methodology">
    <h3>Methodology</h3>
    <p>
      <strong>Rookie pool</strong>: every FantasyCalc-valued player with
      <code>years_exp = 0</code> (entering their first NFL season) who isn't
      currently on a roster in your league.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Projected availability</strong> assumes other managers will
      pick strictly by FantasyCalc dynasty value descending. At overall
      pick N, the algorithm shows rookies ranked #N through #N+7. Reality
      will diverge — TEs and QBs tend to fall further than their ranking,
      RBs often go earlier in superflex / 1-QB formats, etc.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Slot value</strong> comes from FantasyCalc's per-slot pick
      values. Earlier picks (1.01, 1.02) are worth more because the player
      pool is steeper at the top.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Limitations:</strong> No positional-need modeling per
      opposing team. No model of draft-day surprises (combine risers,
      trades, news). Assumes 10-team draft ordering — multi-team formats
      would need slot remapping.
    </p>
  </div>

  <footer class="site">
    Data: <a href="https://docs.sleeper.com">Sleeper</a> &middot;
    <a href="https://fantasycalc.com">FantasyCalc</a>.
  </footer>
</div>
</body>
</html>
